  "narrative": "The new batch of discovery results is important for narrowing the feature_021 follow-up and completing two controlled predictor screens. For outcome_014, the clinical threshold implied by the outcome mean magnitude is about 0.0093. H104 tests feature_021=1 versus 0 within feature_027=0 and gives a signed estimate of -0.00078 (95% interval -0.0213 to +0.0197; cell sizes 321 and 1286). This is essentially null in the larger feature_027=0 stratum and does not support a broad positive feature_021-outcome_014 association. H105 within feature_027=1 gives a positive point estimate of +0.01685, but its 95% interval is wide (-0.0307 to +0.0644) and includes both zero and clinically meaningful values. H106, the corresponding feature_027 interaction, is also large and imprecise (+0.0176; interval -0.0340 to +0.0693). H107, testing feature_021 within feature_050=0, gives +0.0136 but with a wide interval (-0.0323 to +0.0595), and H108, the feature_050 interaction, is very imprecise (+0.0107; interval -0.0866 to +0.1080). Taken together, these results argue against accepting feature_021 as a robust secondary outcome_014 marker in the supplied dataset. The unstratified H101 result remains near threshold but imprecise, and the subgroup evidence is not convergent: one key stratum is null and the positive strata are uncertain. I therefore do not accept any feature_021 outcome_014 claim, leave the individual feature_021 claims unresolved and deferred, and move H101 off the active set. For outcome_001, H109, H111, and H113 test feature_021, feature_012, and feature_020 within feature_050=0 with negative-direction claims. Their upper bounds (+0.0119, +0.0286, and +0.0148) are all well below the outcome_001 clinical threshold of about 0.0415, so each rejects a clinically meaningful stronger-dependency association within that complement. The corresponding outcome_014 controlled screens for feature_012 and feature_020 within feature_027=0 are near zero (+0.00285 and +0.00087), though their upper bounds exceed the small outcome_014 threshold, so they remain unresolved rather than accepted. H64, feature_045 for outcome_014 in the negative direction, gives a signed estimate opposite to the registered direction (-0.0218) with an upper bound just above threshold (+0.0153); this is not compelling and remains unresolved. H65, feature_042 for outcome_014 in the positive direction, has upper bound +0.0012, clearly below the +0.0093 threshold, and is rejected. Overall, the strongest dataset-specific associations remain the already accepted very large feature_027-outcome_014 shift and the feature_050-outcome_001 stronger-dependency association. I request no validation now because no new candidate has an interval lower bound above clinical significance and no candidate shows enough convergence to justify one of the remaining validation comparisons. All conclusions are associations within defined strata of the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, mechanism, or generalizability.",
