  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 appraise after feature_021 robustness and controlled predictor screens. The new evidence strongly weakens feature_021 as a broad secondary outcome_014 marker: H104 in feature_027=0 is near null (-0.0008; interval -0.0213 to +0.0197), while H105 in feature_027=1 is positive but imprecise (+0.0168; interval -0.0307 to +0.0644). The feature_027 interaction H106 and feature_050-controlled feature_021 results H107/H108 are also wide and do not converge enough to support acceptance. H101 remains unresolved but deferred. Outcome_001 controlled screens reject clinically meaningful negative associations within feature_050=0 for feature_021 (H109), feature_012 (H111), and feature_020 (H113) because upper bounds are far below the outcome_001 threshold about 0.0415. Controlled outcome_014 screens for feature_012 and feature_020 within feature_027=0 are near null; their upper bounds still cross the small outcome_014 threshold about 0.0093, so they remain unresolved deferred. H64 feature_045 outcome_014 negative-direction is opposite at point estimate but has upper bound above threshold, so unresolved; H65 feature_042 outcome_014 positive-direction is rejected because upper bound is below threshold. Central accepted dataset-specific associations remain H14/H14-like feature_027-outcome_014 and H88/H96/H97 feature_050-outcome_001. No new validation is requested because no new claim has interval lower bound above clinical significance or enough subgroup convergence. Future priority is broad exploration rather than feature_021, unless a new analysis provides a clean lower bound above threshold in a preregistered stratum. All statements remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
